# vms-b0f (via vms-35b): SHOW MEMORY section/column LAYOUT on OpenVMS VAX V7.3.
# NON-deterministic (free/modified pages, cache, dynamic-memory bytes, paging-file
# counts, and the header timestamp all vary run-to-run), so it uses the digit-mask
# NORMALIZE: every digit -> '#', which preserves column width/alignment while
# masking the volatile values. The golden is thus the reproducible LAYOUT (section
# headers, column headers, row labels, geometry). The vms-c38 gate applies the
# SAME mask to OVMX's SHOW MEMORY before diffing:
#   capture_oracle.sh normalize vax-show-memory < ovmx_show_memory_output
#
# MAY_OMIT (vms-c38, GROUNDED substrate-absent sections) -- diff_surface strips
# these whole sections from BOTH the golden and OVMX before the MATCH compare, so
# OVMX honestly omitting a facility the substrate genuinely lacks is faithful, not
# a red. Each entry is grounded in the acceptance battery's EXISTING, reviewed
# must_not_have assertions (a reviewed reality, not a new hole):
#   - "Virtual I/O Cache Usage" -- no XFC (extended file cache) on the substrate;
#      dcl_acceptance_battery.sh: must_not_have 'Virtual I/O Cache Usage'.
#   - "Slot Usage"              -- no VMS balance-set slot table on the substrate;
#      dcl_acceptance_battery.sh: must_not_have 'Slot Usage'.
# ⚠ MAY_OMIT is for substrate-ABSENT facilities ONLY. A section OVMX could source
# but doesn't render (e.g. if Physical Memory went missing) stays a real HOLLOW
# gap and MUST red -- never add it here to silence a genuine divergence (INV-6).
ARCH=vax
DESC="SHOW MEMORY section/column layout (digit-masked; free/pages/times volatile)"
NORMALIZE='s/[0-9]/#/g'
MAY_OMIT='Virtual I/O Cache Usage|Slot Usage'
COMMANDS=(
  'SHOW MEMORY'
)
